\section{The four formulas}{

The frame R' moves at a constant speed \code{v} along the x axis relative to R.
\itemize{
\item Position: \verb{x' = x - v * t}
\item Time: \verb{t' = t}
\item Velocity: \verb{u = u' + v}
\item Acceleration: \verb{a' = a}
}

These formulas hold when speeds are very small compared with the speed
of light.
}

